{"name":"Poodle Skirt","hex":"#ffaebb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poodle skirt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wide felt knee-length skirt of a solid bold colour displaying a design appliquéd or transferred to the fabric, originally of a coiffed French poodle; popular in the United States in the 1950s."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poodle_skirt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poodle skirt","blocks":[{"text":"A poodle skirt is a wide swing felt skirt of a solid color displaying a design appliquéd or transferred to the fabric. The design was often a coiffed poodle. Later substitutes for the poodle patch included flamingoes, flowers, and hot rod cars. They quickly became very popular with teenage girls in 1950s, who wore them at school dances, and as everyday wear."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d0/The_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Poodle_skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poodle_skirt","wikidata":"Q4120618"},{"title":"Poodle","blocks":[{"text":"The Poodle, called the Pudel in German and the Caniche in French, is a breed of water dog. The breed is divided into four varieties based on size, the Standard Poodle, Medium Poodle, Miniature Poodle and Toy Poodle, although the Medium Poodle is not universally recognised. They have a distinctive thick, curly coat that comes in many colours and patterns, with only solid colours recognised by major breed registries. Poodles are active and intelligent, and are particularly able to learn from humans. Poodles tend to live 10–18 years, with smaller varieties tending to live longer than larger ones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Full_attention_%288067543690%29.jpg/330px-Full_attention_%288067543690%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poodle","wikidata":"Q38904"},{"title":"Skirt","blocks":[{"text":"A skirt is the lower part of a dress or a separate outer garment that covers a person from the waist downwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Skirt.jpg/330px-Skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skirt","wikidata":"Q2160801"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Girl_wearing_poodle_skirt.jpg/500px-Girl_wearing_poodle_skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Girl_wearing_poodle_skirt.jpg/500px-Girl_wearing_poodle_skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Girl wearing saddle shoes and a poodle skirt","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGirl_wearing_poodle_skirt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/PoodleSkirtTwirl.jpg/330px-PoodleSkirtTwirl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/PoodleSkirtTwirl.jpg/330px-PoodleSkirtTwirl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"When spinning, the skirt would flare out.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoodleSkirtTwirl.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/1950s_poodle_skirts.jpg/500px-1950s_poodle_skirts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/1950s_poodle_skirts.jpg/500px-1950s_poodle_skirts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The decorations could be chosen to reflect the wearer's interests.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1950s_poodle_skirts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.